/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Continuous Integration \(CI\) is a fundamental practice in DevOps, ensuring that code changes are automatically built, tested, and merged into the main branch frequently. Jenkins, a popular open-source automation server, facilitates CI by automating these processes. This chapter delves into setting up Jenkins, creating CI pipelines, and provides real-life examples, coded examples with output, illustrations, cheat sheets, and case studies to illustrate effective CI practices.  4.1 Introduction to Jenkins )
/E (Continuous Integration \(CI\) is a fundamental practice in DevOps, ensuring that code changes are automatically built, tested, and merged into the main branch frequently. Jenkins, a popular open-source automation server, facilitates CI by automating these processes. This chapter delves into setting up Jenkins, creating CI pipelines, and provides real-life examples, coded examples with output, illustrations, cheat sheets, and case studies to illustrate effective CI practices.  4.1 Introduction to Jenkins )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
